### Round 2, fifth batch (release `shots-b7`): even cadence
Wan's output moves on about every other frame (an effective ~13 fps in 30 fps frames; `decimate` could not undo that). Every `shots/*_wan*.mp4` is re-converted from the raw Wan file with a 5-frame weighted temporal mix and a blend resample to 24 fps (`tmix=frames=5:weights=1 2 3 2 1,framerate=fps=24`; tools/wan.py), no audio. The alternation measure (tools/cad.py, alt2 as in director's table) falls: s18b 0.34 -> 0.05, s14b 0.21 -> 0.05, s04_wan1 0.18 -> 0.09, s17 0.09 -> 0.05, s16 0.17 -> 0.06, s15_wan2 0.14 -> 0.06, s19 0.19 -> 0.09, s13a_wan2 0.12 -> 0.04, s10 0.17 -> 0.06, s12 0.09 -> 0.05. Same names, same durations (within one frame). Two extra slow-prompt takes of the finding and the plea: `shots/s18d_wan1.mp4`, `s18d_wan2.mp4` (1080P source), `shots/s14c_wan1.mp4` (not needed unless the editor prefers them).
